            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of painful osteoporosis with fluoride, calcium, and calciferol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fourteen women averaging 69.5 years of age with painful osteoporosis of the spine were treated with sodium fluoride, calcium salts and calciferol. At assessment after 5-19 months of therapy 8 patients were free of pains while in 5 women pains had decreased and mobility improved. One patient had unaltered pains. Side effects were few and mild.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
